 "rule_tried": {
  "definition": "for every set-piece window without a D of the decision in [start - 5 s, end): the frame of that region through which the decoder passes D at the least cost (forward-backward scores of the unchanged v2 decoder); if that cost is at most c (log units; one D run costs 120 in transitions), the decoder is re-run with that frame forced to D, which also settles the extent of the run. Variants: other c, search region from 3 s / 8 s before or up to 2 s after the window, runs widened to 1 s, short possession pieces between the forced run and the next team change written D (bridge)",
  "simulated_tags": "windows [restart - U(0.5, 4) s, restart + U(1, 5) s] as in possession-v3-plan.json, kept with the published per-type rates times a scale, start and end shifted by lag + N(0, sigma); false windows of 3-7 s on live frames. Regimes: {\"clean\": {\"scale\": [1, 1], \"lag\": [0, 0], \"sigma\": [0.3, 0.3], \"false\": [0, 0]}, \"default\": {\"scale\": [0.5, 1.5], \"lag\": [-1.5, 1.5], \"sigma\": [0.3, 3.0], \"false\": [0, 0.15]}, \"noisy\": {\"scale\": [0.5, 0.5], \"lag\": [1.5, 1.5], \"sigma\": [3.0, 3.0], \"false\": [0.15, 0.15]}, \"false30\": {\"scale\": [0.5, 1.5], \"lag\": [-1.5, 1.5], \"sigma\": [0.3, 3.0], \"false\": [0.3, 0.3]}, \"second\": {\"scale\": [1, 1], \"lag\": [0, 0], \"sigma\": [1.0, 1.0], \"false\": [0.05, 0.05]}} (scale, lag s, sigma s, false windows as a share of the tags; pairs are uniform ranges); seeds 910000 + 1000 * regime index + copy index",
